WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.710
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.100
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.100
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.410
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.920
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.620
You're right. Thank goodness.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:49.880
Everyone!

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:57.530
Episode 39

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:57.530
The Chaotix Detective Agency

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.610
So far, they've appeared in five locations around the city.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:19.490
Most of them are at the Mystic Ruins.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:23.200
And those creatures were inside?

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.080
The name of this bird is Flicky.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:32.290
Flicky and the others are from the same world as Sonic?

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.630
Most likely.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:41.390
What do Sonic and Tails think about this incident?

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:43.890
You don't need to beat around the bush.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:51.520
When you asked for just me and Chris, I had an idea what you were concerned about.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.400
Excuse us for being rude. However...

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.900
Don't get me wrong.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.650
I'm grateful for your thoughtfulness.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.490
I'm sure Chris understands too.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.790
You're saying we should live together?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.790
We don't even know each other that well.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.710
It could be trouble.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:27.220
If two people who've been living entirely different lives start living together...

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.680
I'm sure many conflicts will arise.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.730
Are you good during the night?

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.110
Stop asking me disturbing questions!

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:39.610
It's not like we're going to be together!

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.990
Oh my, just what are you thinking?

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.070
I'm a bat, and bats are good during the night.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.910
I was just wondering if you were or not.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.950
Don't you prefer dark places?

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:57.420
Anyway, there hasn't been a huge commotion.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:05.300
Yeah. The instant they appeared in the city, GUN took them to the Mystic Ruins.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.430
It's like a cover-up.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.810
They had no choice.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:13.600
Or did you have a better idea?

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:18.150
Did you have an idea that would've prevented the people from panicking?

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.860
Anyway, since it's okay with you, I'll think about it.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:23.950
Think about what?

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.490
About us living together.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.410
You gotta be joking!

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.330
Idiot!

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:53.390
It's already late.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:55.560
We should hurry home for Ella's cooking-

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:55.980
- Grandpa.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.440
Is it impossible?

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.530
If people are from two different worlds...

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.660
Is it impossible for us to live together in peace?

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.040
Chris.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:24.720
Because Shadow sacrificed himself so that everyone could be happy.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.510
Chris…

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:39.230
He's late!

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:42.980
How long is Charmy going to take?

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.780
Things aren't that simple, Vector.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:52.450
Where are we, and why I are we here?

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.620
Can you explain that?

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:59.460
There's no doubt that we were sent somewhere.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:03.590
Did we warp through time or through space?

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.920
Which is more likely?

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.470
I think warping through time is more likely.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.600
However, there's one thing that's strange.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.020
Something strange?

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.060
Half of the moon is missing!

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:24.530
I'm shocked!

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.780
I'm super shocked!

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:30.570
Don't let this shock you, even though I know it's gonna!

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.370
What's so shocking?

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:36.620
This isn't our world!

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.210
Look at the newspaper from this world!

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.040
Charmy.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:40.750
It says that-

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.040
Charmy!

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:42.750
What?

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:46.170
Get off of my nose!

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:49.220
So where are we?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:49.970
I don't know!

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:55.390
You've been flying around since this morning, and that's all you have?

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.690
What's with that arrogant 'tsk tsk tsk' hand motion?

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.360
That's why I've been trying to tell you to look at this.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.440
Oops, that's the wrong article.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:06.860
You did that on purpose.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.110
Here!

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:10.530
Isn't that...

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.780
That's Sonic!

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:17.450
What's this? 'Our Sonic has done it again!'

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.710
'He risked his life to stop the ARK from falling.'

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.880
What's an ARK, and what do they mean by 'he did it again?'

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.130
What's he done in this world?

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.670
Furthermore...

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.010
What's that?

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:34.800
Sonic's heroic deeds are in this movie.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.390
Dolby Digital 5.1 surround sound, Hi-spec version.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.730
Stop reading what's written there.

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:45.060
He's making his presence known in this world too.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:48.360
Wow! This high-spec version has special bonus footage!

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.780
Knuckles changes into a sexy swimsuit on a southern island.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.360
Who the hell wants to see something like that?

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.030
Where did you find that anyway?

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:58.240
Lots of places were selling them.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:01.120
It's worth checking out.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:09.760
We may find out why we ended up here.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:11.970
What's this?

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.050
How do we watch what's on here?

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:22.270
You need a special device.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:27.060
I understand!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.190
This is horrible.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:37.660
I'm using my powers for this?

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:40.200
I'm no better than a thief.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.770
<i>I will return it.
 -Espio</i>

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.920
Well done, Espio. You finish missions quickly.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.260
Yeah.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:59.180
Now let's watch what the superhero does.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:01.720
The TVs in this world are really thin.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.740
Fast forward through the opening.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:22.200
Fine, I'll watch it later.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:46.020
Knuckles, can you hear me?

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:50.520
I’m going to destroy this robot. Stay safely away.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.080
It's my turn. Go!

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:23.850
Can you hear me?

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.060
Yeah!

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.230
I can hear you!

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.440
Chaos...

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.190
...Control!

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:54.380
Maria, is this what you wanted?

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:03.350
I see. Chaos Control.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:08.680
No wonder I couldn't find him.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:12.230
You mean he's hiding somewhere in this world?

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:15.520
There's no doubt about that.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:19.860
Hey, how are you all doing? I'm here at a southern island.

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:23.120
Don't show us that!

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:27.040
Oops, I almost forgot!

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:30.160
My name's Vector the Crocodile!

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:33.670
I'm the president of the Chaotix detective agency.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:39.050
I may be quick to fight and have a sharp tongue, but I'm also tenderhearted and honorable.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:44.850
And don't group me with those characters who only have brute strength.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:49.810
Despite my appearance, I'm a cunning detective who solves most of our cases.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.310
Yay! I'm Ch-

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.270
I'm Espio the Chameleon.

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.610
I'm the agency's analyst.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:02.150
Unlike the silly nature of the others, I'm calm and collected.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:07.030
No matter how dangerous the task, there's nothing I can't overcome with my ninja skills.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:09.950
I live and die in the shadows.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:11.750
That's my credo.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.870
Then don't appear!

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:20.090
If I let you act so arrogantly, it will destroy this agency's morals.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.840
You're also supposed to respect your superiors!

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.720
Haven't you heard of first-come, first-served?

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.260
In that case, I was born before you.

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.230
That's now what I meant by who was first!

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.730
C'mon Espio, that's enough.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:37.690
Charmy, say hi to the viewers.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:40.000
I'm-

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:10.760
Mr. President, a rocket has launched from Eggman's former base.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:13.770
Where is the rocket heading towards?

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:14.770
Confirming position!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:18.360
The rocket that was launched from Eggman's base is heading towards the moon!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.320
It's flying towards the moon!

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:23.740
Why does this have to happen now?

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:24.780
Mr. President!

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:26.360
What is it now?

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:29.370
You have a video call from Dr. Eggman.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:37.330
I'm sorry I scared you with that ARK incident.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:42.590
As a token of my apology, I'm going to repair the moon free of charge.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:46.340
The moon looks better when it's round, right?

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:49.090
Repair the moon?

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:53.220
I can't return it to its original state, but I can at least repair the shape.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:57.600
I hope you understand that I really feel bad about what I did.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.310
Can you trace the call?

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:03.230
What's come over Eggman?

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:07.110
Do you really think he's doing this because he feels apologetic?

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:10.740
I hope so.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:13.080
What? You successfully traced the call?

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.290
Really?

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.750
I want to talk to him! Make contact!

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.790
95 Riverside?

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:24.800
That's ridiculous! That's my house!

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:27.800
Let's not be naive.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:05.590
Eggman destroyed the moon, but he has now repaired it back to its original shape.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.130
It only took ten minutes to repair the moon.

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:10.470
His scientific capabilities is amazing.

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:14.100
But half of it looks like a Christmas tree.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:18.480
Why is Sonic always missing at a time like this?

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:21.020
What's that?

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:27.780
All right, we're going to solve our client's case today.

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:30.610
Are you sure you want to say something like that?

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:34.570
That's right. There's no guarantee that it's in this world.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.410
I always find the truth!

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.160
I have the brains of a genius and the appearance of a crocodile!

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:42.710
I'm the great Detective Vector!

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:45.790
Of course you look like a crocodile. What are you talking about?

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:48.760
He was watching this world's anime channel until the morning.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.800
I'd like to ask you one question.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:54.470
Is this from another TV show?

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.050
From a detective series.

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.220
You see, my wife…

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:00.560
How long are you going to keep this up, Vector?

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:09.070
Chaos Control sent the thing we're searching for into this world, along with Sonic.

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.570
What makes you so confident?

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:13.860
Have my instincts ever failed?

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.820
This is based just on your instincts?

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.950
Don't compare my instincts to anyone else's!

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.950
Vector's instincts are number one in the universe!

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.040
Bingo!

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:29.250
Just as I thought, Sonic kidnapped it.

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:33.760
It only took one scene transition to find Sonic's house. Are we that pressed for time?

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:37.390
That's one reason, but his house was also on a map of rich people's houses.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.470
Why's that?

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:45.520
People in this world like to peer into the lives of those that they envy.

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:46.480
How stupid.

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:51.440
Sonic tricked a rich family to take him in. That's unforgivable!

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:52.280
Are you jealous?

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.070
A little.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:54.780
How dare you make me say that, Charmy!

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.160
But you love money!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:02.910
Don't get me wrong. I may love money, but I won't do anything illegal to get it.

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:05.790
Let's hurry up and rescue it.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:09.540
Our job is to give our client peace of mind as fast as possible.

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:12.710
Don't get impatient. This mansion is huge.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:14.880
It'll have tight security.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:18.220
If they had security, wouldn't they have found us by now?

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:20.850
Look!

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.850
They have a super powerful security guard!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:28.270
You're right. I'll be so scared that I'll forget to run away.

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:31.190
The guard looked in our direction!

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:33.490
What should we do? Should we quit?

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:34.860
Stop joking around!

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.740
This is exactly when...

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.240
We take action.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.840
Eggman?

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:55.630
Sonic.

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:59.970
Do you have time to chat?

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.310
Well done, as always.

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:11.940
With Espio's foliage hiding ninja technique, there's no place he can't sneak into!

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:14.190
Sheesh, Sonic!

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:17.110
He said he'd be back by noon. What a liar!

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:18.780
This is normal.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:23.120
He won't get away with this! I'll punish him today!

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.120
Amy...

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:30.040
Why did I feel like I just hit something?

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.380
E-Espio!

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.050
I failed.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:42.050
I didn't know that girl was also a co-conspirator.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:43.510
Espio!

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:45.520
How dare they!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:47.100
What are you going to do?

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:49.140
We're going to use our power!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.150
We'll fight them face-to-face!

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.520
Yeah! Fight!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.650
You offered to repair the moon.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:00.700
What's come over you?

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:03.910
It's no big deal.

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:07.580
If I go home and leave things as is, then I'll feel like I owe a debt.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.330
That doesn't feel good.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:10.790
Go home?

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.920
I know you understand.

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:19.340
Do you think this will last forever?

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.340
I don't really think about it.

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:22.970
I know you're having a good time.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:29.390
You're having a good time living with them everyday.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:36.230
If people from our world keep coming to this world, there's going to be friction.

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:40.450
That's not necessarily true.

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:45.030
I can see right through you, Sonic.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:48.240
You just don't want to think about it.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.370
You're acting strange yourself!

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:53.670
You're like an old man that can't stop talking.

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:54.830
Umm...

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:56.750
You're…

00:19:57.880 --> 00:19:59.710
What?

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:03.260
Aren't you being a bit cruel?

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.800
Yeah, cruel!

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.260
Cruel about what?

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:08.470
Tails, do you know them?

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:11.850
Who are you anyway?

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:16.560
That's not important! Now calmly give us Cream back!

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:17.940
We'll take it!

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:21.400
Huh? You're going to return me?

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:24.200
Are they dangerous?

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.030
I don't know...

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:28.580
So you've brought out the guard!

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:31.410
Then we're also going to use our super weapon!

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:33.830
This stinger hurts!

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.500
What?

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.880
What the heck are you talking about?

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:39.960
You punks!

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:45.800
What's with the racket?

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:48.050
Sonic, great timing!

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:50.850
The kidnapper finally showed up!

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:53.560
Kidnapper? What do you mean by that?

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:57.940
You're…

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.730
Thank you for everything, Vector.

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:03.860
Hey Cream! You have a lovely guest.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:16.710
I searched everywhere for you, Cream.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:24.170
Mo… Mo…

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:26.840
Mommy!

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:28.600
Cream!

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.970
Mommy!

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:36.190
I'm happy. I'm so happy.

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:39.310
It's Cream's mother.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:45.610
Thank you, Vector.

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:48.200
No problem. It's my job.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:53.870
And Sonic, thank you for taking care of Cream all this time. I don't know how to thank you.

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:55.710
Take care? Thank?

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:57.370
What does this mean, Vector?

00:21:57.370 --> 00:22:00.670
You were saying something about a kidnapping?

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:04.090
Oh my, Sonic! What are you doing here?

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:07.680
Charmy, let's go to our next job.

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:09.430
You don't need to play dumb.

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:11.050
Let's have a nice, long talk.

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:13.140
That's right! What did you mean when you said we were cruel?

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:17.190
What are you all talking about? You're all weird.

00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:19.190
You're the weirdo.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:29.700
Should you be laughing?

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:33.950
There's no way I'd repair the moon for nothing!

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:39.540
There will be big trouble next week!

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:44.380
Ouch...

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:54.510
<b>Watashitachi no sekai wa mahou o kakerarete</b>

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:54.510
<i>There’s magic cast on our world.</i>

00:22:54.510 --> 00:23:03.480
<b>Ai suru to kime kisae namida ni ujirareteru</b>

00:22:54.510 --> 00:23:03.480
<i>The nervousness of love is sealed by tears.</i>

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:12.370
<b>Boy boy futari de jumon wo sagashi ni ikou</b>

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:12.370
<i>Boy, let’s search for a spell together,</i>

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:21.960
<b>Kinji rareta yume wo kanaerareru kuni he</b>

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:21.960
<i>To a land where our forbidden dreams can come true.</i>

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:30.930
<b>Dare ni mo naisho de ashita na tchi awaseshiyou</b>

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:30.930
<i>Let’s secretly meet tomorrow.</i>

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:41.100
<b>Itsuka kotori wo ume ta yowake no mieru oka de</b>

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:41.100
<i>At the place where we buried the bird, the hill where we can see the sunrise.</i>

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:49.860
<b>Tsumetai asamoya kimi to te wo tsunaidara</b>

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:49.860
<i>In the cold morning mist, if I hold hands with you.</i>

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:59.040
<b>Hikaru michi no fuuin ga tokeru yo</b>

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:59.040
<i>The seal to the shining path will be broken.</i>

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:03.880
<b>Hateshinaku</b>

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:03.880
<i>Forever...</i>

00:24:30.760 --> 00:25:35.430
Eggman Company
